title: $:/plugins/btheado/notebook-kit/examples/nested-modules

<$testcase>
  <$data $tiddler="$:/plugins/btheado/notebook-kit"/>
  <$data title="Parent cell" type="application/javascript" text=`const duplicate = "parent";
display("parent module: " + duplicate);`/>
  <$data title="Child cell" type="application/javascript" text=`const duplicate = "child";
display("child module: " + duplicate);`/>
  <$data title=ChildNotebook text="""<$notebook-kit>
  <div class="tc-notebook-output" data-tiddler-title="Child cell"/>
</$notebook-kit>"""/>
  <$data title=Output text="""<$notebook-kit>
  <div class="tc-notebook-output" data-tiddler-title="Parent cell"/>
  <$transclude tiddler=ChildNotebook/>
  <$transclude tiddler=ChildNotebook/>
</$notebook-kit>"""/>
</$testcase>

This parent notebook and both inline child instances define `duplicate`. Each
child receives its own Observable module, so all three outputs render without
duplicate-name errors.
